# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Internal design docs — kept out of the public repository (temporary)
docs/

# Pulumi
Pulumi.*.yaml.bak
.pulumi/

# Build output. Pulumi's go language host compiles each layer to a stable
# path under here so repeated previews skip the link step.
.cache/

# Task. The remote lock is the exception and is committed on purpose: it pins
# the CONTENT behind the `?ref=vX.Y.Z` tag, so a moved tag stops the build
# instead of silently changing it. Refresh deliberately with `task --download`.
.task/*
!.task/remote/
.task/remote/*
!.task/remote/*.checksum

# Cluster credentials produced by `task cluster:kubeconfig` / `cluster:talosconfig`
kubeconfig
talosconfig
*.kubeconfig

# Local etcd snapshots
.backups/

# Compiled output. `go build -o bin/ ./...` — what `task build` and the CI
# priming job run — puts every binary here, so the repository root stays clean
# and this is one line instead of a list.
bin/

# A bare `go build ./...` still drops a binary named after each main package
# into the working directory, and those names collide with the tools/, layers/
# and infra/ directory names. The names below cover that; the pre-commit
# forbid-binaries hook is what actually guarantees none is committed, because
# it asks git rather than matching a name.
#
# TestGitignore_CoversEveryBinaryName derives this list from the tree, because
# a hand-maintained one went stale three times: twice for a new tool, and once
# for `infra/cluster`, whose binary is called `cluster`.
/alloyvalidate
/awk
/charts
/cluster
/imagebake
/render
/stack
/talosvalidate
/topology
/[0-9][0-9]-*

# Local-only lefthook overrides. Gates that belong to a working copy rather
# than to the project; lefthook merges the file automatically when present.
lefthook-local.yml

# Stack topologies. Kept local: adminCIDRs is the operator's own egress
# address, and this repository is public. cluster.example.yaml is the committed
# template — copy it to cluster.<stack>.yaml.
infra/cluster/cluster.*.yaml
!infra/cluster/cluster.example.yaml
